#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:3
msgid "激活函数"
msgstr "Activation Functions"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:5
msgid "激活函数的本质：划分特征空间"
msgstr "Essence of Activation Functions: Partitioning Feature Space"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:7
msgid "从线性回归到逻辑回归"
msgstr "From Linear Regression to Logistic Regression"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:9
msgid ""
"你可能熟悉**线性回归**：$y = wx + "
"b$，它用一条直线拟合数据，输出连续值。但很多时候我们需要做**分类**——不是预测数值，而是判断\"这是A类还是B类\"。"
msgstr ""
"You may be familiar with **linear regression**: $y = wx + b$, which fits data using a straight line and outputs continuous values. However, in many cases we need to perform **classification**—predicting not continuous values, but deciding whether something belongs to \"Class A or Class B\"."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:11
msgid "**问题**：如果用线性回归做二分类会怎样？"
msgstr "**Question**: What happens if we use linear regression for binary classification?"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:13
msgid ""
"假设我们想区分\"垃圾邮件\"和\"正常邮件\"。如果用线性回归输出 $y = wx + "
"b$，我们得到一个实数值。但分类需要的是一个概率——\"这封邮件是垃圾邮件的可能性有多大\"。"
msgstr ""
"Suppose we want to distinguish \"spam emails\" from \"legitimate emails\". If we use linear regression output $y = wx + b$, we get a real value. But classification requires a probability—\"how likely is this email to be spam?\""

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:15
msgid "**逻辑回归**解决了这个问题。它在线性回归的输出上叠加一个 **Sigmoid** 函数："
msgstr "**Logistic regression** solves this problem by applying a **Sigmoid** function over the linear regression output:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:17
msgid "\\hat{y} = \\sigma(wx + b) = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-(wx + b)}}"
msgstr "\\hat{y} = \\sigma(wx + b) = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-(wx + b)}}"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:19
msgid "Sigmoid 将任意实数压缩到 $(0, 1)$ 区间，恰好可以解释为概率。"
msgstr "Sigmoid squashes any real number into the $(0, 1)$ interval, which can be interpreted directly as a probability."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:21
msgid "**逻辑回归的决策规则**："
msgstr "**Decision Rule of Logistic Regression**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:23
msgid "如果 $\\sigma(wx + b) \\geq 0.5$，预测为类别1"
msgstr "If $\\sigma(wx + b) \\geq 0.5$, predict Class 1"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:24
msgid "如果 $\\sigma(wx + b) < 0.5$，预测为类别0"
msgstr "If $\\sigma(wx + b) < 0.5$, predict Class 0"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:26
msgid ""
"这等价于判断 $wx + b \\geq 0$ 还是 $wx + b < "
"0$——在特征空间中，就是用一条**直线**（或超平面）划分两个区域。逻辑回归只能学习**线性决策边界**。"
msgstr ""
"This is equivalent to checking whether $wx + b \\geq 0$ or $wx + b < 0$—which in feature space means partitioning two regions using a **straight line** (or hyperplane). Logistic regression can only learn **linear decision boundaries**."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:28
msgid "为什么需要激活函数"
msgstr "Why We Need Activation Functions"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:30
msgid "逻辑回归解决了二分类问题，但它有一个根本限制：**只能学习线性边界**。现实中很多分类问题的决策边界是复杂的非线性形状——比如异或（XOR）问题，逻辑回归就无法解决。"
msgstr "Logistic regression solves binary classification, but has a fundamental limitation: **it can only learn linear boundaries**. In reality, decision boundaries for many classification problems have complex non-linear shapes—such as the XOR problem, which logistic regression cannot solve."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:32
msgid "**多层感知机（MLP）** 突破了这个限制："
msgstr "**Multilayer Perceptrons (MLPs)** break through this limitation:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:34
msgid "第一层：多个神经元并行，各自学习不同的线性边界"
msgstr "First layer: Multiple neurons in parallel, each learning a different linear boundary"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:35
msgid "**激活函数**：引入非线性，将空间\"折叠\""
msgstr "**Activation functions**: Introduce non-linearity to \"fold\" space"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:36
msgid "后续层：组合这些折叠后的特征，学习复杂边界"
msgstr "Subsequent layers: Combine these folded features to learn complex boundaries"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:38
msgid "什么是\"空间\"？"
msgstr "What is \"Space\"?"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:40
msgid "在深度学习中，**空间**指的是输入数据的特征空间："
msgstr "In deep learning, **space** refers to the feature space of input data:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:42
msgid "一个样本对应空间中的一个**点**"
msgstr "A sample corresponds to a **point** in space"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:43
msgid "每个特征对应一个**坐标轴**"
msgstr "Each feature corresponds to a **coordinate axis**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:44
msgid "MNIST 图像（784维）就是784维空间中的点"
msgstr "An MNIST image (784 dimensions) is a point in a 784-dimensional space"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:46
msgid "神经网络的每一层都在**变换这个空间**："
msgstr "Every layer of a neural network is **transforming this space**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:48
msgid "线性变换（$Wx + b$）：旋转、缩放、平移"
msgstr "Linear transformation ($Wx + b$): Rotation, scaling, translation"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:49
msgid "**非线性激活**：将空间\"折叠\"，使线性不可分的数据变得可分"
msgstr "**Non-linear activation**: \"Folds\" space, making linearly inseparable data separable"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:53
msgid "决策边界的形成"
msgstr "Formation of Decision Boundaries"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:55
msgid ""
"没有激活函数，无论堆叠多少层，网络只能学习线性变换——因为多个线性变换的组合仍然是线性的：$f(W_2(W_1x)) = W_2W_1x = "
"W'x$。激活函数引入非线性，使网络能够在空间中划分**复杂的决策边界**。"
msgstr ""
"Without activation functions, no matter how many layers are stacked, the network can only learn linear transformations—because the composition of multiple linear transformations remains linear: $f(W_2(W_1x)) = W_2W_1x = W'x$. Activation functions introduce non-linearity, enabling the network to partition **complex decision boundaries** in space."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:64
msgid "3神经元网络形成的复杂决策边界"
msgstr "Complex Decision Boundary Formed by a 3-Neuron Network"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:67
msgid "**网络结构解析**："
msgstr "**Network Architecture Breakdown**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:69
msgid "这个网络只有 3 个隐藏层神经元，却能形成如此复杂的决策边界。让我们逐层解析："
msgstr "This network has only 3 hidden neurons, yet forms such a complex decision boundary. Let us break it down layer by layer:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:84
msgid "**数学表达式**："
msgstr "**Mathematical Expression**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:86
msgid "基础激活函数："
msgstr "Basic activation functions:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:88
msgid "**Swish**: 平滑的 ReLU 变体"
msgstr "**Swish**: Smooth variant of ReLU"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:90
msgid "r(x) = \\frac{x}{1 + e^{-x}}"
msgstr "r(x) = \\frac{x}{1 + e^{-x}}"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:92
msgid "**Sigmoid**: 将值压缩到 0-1"
msgstr "**Sigmoid**: Squashes values into 0–1"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:94
msgid "s(x) = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-x}}"
msgstr "s(x) = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-x}}"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:96
msgid "隐藏层神经元（3 个独立的线性变换 + Swish）："
msgstr "Hidden layer neurons (3 independent linear transformations + Swish):"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:98
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"n_1 &= r(2x - 1) \\quad \\text{[对x敏感的神经元]} \\\\\n"
"n_2 &= r(3x + 1) \\quad \\text{[另一个x方向的神经元]} \\\\\n"
"n_3 &= r(y - 2) \\quad \\text{[对y敏感的神经元]}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"n_1 &= r(2x - 1) \\quad \\text{[Neuron sensitive to x]} \\\\\n"
"n_2 &= r(3x + 1) \\quad \\text{[Another neuron in x direction]} \\\\\n"
"n_3 &= r(y - 2) \\quad \\text{[Neuron sensitive to y]}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:106
msgid "输出决策边界："
msgstr "Output decision boundary:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:108
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\text{决策} = s\\big(\\underbrace{n_2}_{\\text{门控}} \\times "
"\\underbrace{(n_1 + n_3)}_{\\text{特征组合}}\\big) > 0.5\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\text{Decision} = s\\big(\\underbrace{n_2}_{\\text{gating}} \\times "
"\\underbrace{(n_1 + n_3)}_{\\text{feature combo}}\\big) > 0.5\n"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:112
msgid "**为什么能形成复杂形状？**"
msgstr "**Why can it form complex shapes?**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:114
msgid "**每个Swish神经元定义一个\"软\"半平面**："
msgstr "**Each Swish neuron defines a \"soft\" half-plane**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:115
msgid "$n_1 = r(2x-1)$：当 $2x-1 > 0$（即 $x > 0.5$）时显著激活"
msgstr "$n_1 = r(2x-1)$: Significantly activated when $2x-1 > 0$ (i.e., $x > 0.5$)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:116
msgid "$n_3 = r(y-2)$：当 $y > 2$ 时显著激活"
msgstr "$n_3 = r(y-2)$: Significantly activated when $y > 2$"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:117
msgid "注意 Swish 不是简单的 0/1 开关，而是平滑过渡"
msgstr "Note that Swish is not a simple 0/1 switch, but a smooth transition"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:119
msgid "**特征组合 $n_1 + n_3$**："
msgstr "**Feature combination $n_1 + n_3$**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:120
msgid "将两个方向的激活\"叠加\""
msgstr "\"Superimposes\" activations from two directions"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:121
msgid "在 $x > 0.5$ 且 $y > 2$ 的区域最强"
msgstr "Strongest in the region where $x > 0.5$ and $y > 2$"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:123
msgid "**门控机制 $n_2 \\times (\\dots)$**："
msgstr "**Gating mechanism $n_2 \\times (\\dots)$**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:124
msgid "$n_2$ 充当\"开关\"，控制哪些区域可以输出"
msgstr "$n_2$ acts as a \"switch\", controlling which regions can output"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:125
msgid "当 $n_2$ 很小时，无论 $(n_1+n_3)$ 多大，输出都接近0"
msgstr "When $n_2$ is very small, no matter how large $(n_1+n_3)$ is, output remains close to 0"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:127
msgid "**Sigmoid最终决策**："
msgstr "**Sigmoid Final Decision**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:128
msgid "将连续值转换为概率式判断"
msgstr "Converts continuous values into probabilistic judgments"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:129
msgid "$>0.5$ 判定为类别A（紫色区域）"
msgstr "$>0.5$ classified as Class A (purple region)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:131
msgid ""
"**直观理解**：这个网络像是在空间中\"雕刻\"——先用 $n_1, n_3$ 定义一个粗略的区域，再用 $n_2$ "
"进行精细修剪，最终得到不规则的形状。"
msgstr ""
"**Intuitive Understanding**: This network is like \"sculpting\" in space—first defining a coarse region with $n_1, n_3$, then fine-trimming it with $n_2$, ultimately creating an irregular shape."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:133
msgid "*交互式探索：[Desmos](https://www.desmos.com/calculator/gnixzk1jaz)（可以拖动滑块调整参数，观察形状变化）*"
msgstr "*Interactive exploration: [Desmos](https://www.desmos.com/calculator/gnixzk1jaz) (drag sliders to adjust parameters and observe shape changes)*"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:135
msgid "**核心洞察**："
msgstr "**Core Insights**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:137
msgid "从这个3神经元的例子，我们可以看到神经网络划分决策边界的关键机制："
msgstr "From this 3-neuron example, we can see the key mechanisms by which neural networks partition decision boundaries:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:139
msgid "**每个神经元定义一个\"软\"边界**："
msgstr "**Each neuron defines a \"soft\" boundary**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:140
msgid "Swish 激活将线性边界 $wx + b = 0$ 变成平滑的过渡区域"
msgstr "Swish activation turns the linear boundary $wx + b = 0$ into a smooth transition region"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:141
msgid "不同于 ReLU 的硬开关，Swish 提供渐变的激活强度"
msgstr "Unlike ReLU's hard switch, Swish provides a gradual activation intensity"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:142
msgid "这允许网络学习更平滑、更复杂的边界"
msgstr "This allows the network to learn smoother, more complex boundaries"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:144
msgid "**非线性组合创造复杂性**："
msgstr "**Non-linear combinations create complexity**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:145
msgid "乘法操作 $n_2 \\times (n_1 + n_3)$ 是关键"
msgstr "The multiplication operation $n_2 \\times (n_1 + n_3)$ is key"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:146
msgid "没有激活函数的非线性，这样的组合无法实现"
msgstr "Without non-linear activation functions, such combinations would be impossible"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:147
msgid "这展示了**非线性激活的本质作用**：让简单线性边界的组合产生复杂形状"
msgstr "This demonstrates the **essential role of non-linear activation**: allowing combinations of simple linear boundaries to generate complex shapes"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:149
msgid "**\"门控\"与\"特征\"的配合**："
msgstr "**Interplay between \"Gating\" and \"Features\"**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:150
msgid "$n_1, n_3$ 提供基础特征（对x和y的响应）"
msgstr "$n_1, n_3$ provide base features (responses to x and y)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:151
msgid "$n_2$ 充当门控，决定哪些区域可以\"通过\""
msgstr "$n_2$ acts as a gate, deciding which regions can \"pass through\""

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:152
msgid "这种配合模式在深层网络中反复出现"
msgstr "This co-working pattern recurs throughout deep networks"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:154
msgid "**少量神经元就能实现复杂分类**："
msgstr "**Complex classification with very few neurons**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:155
msgid "仅需3个神经元就能形成非凸、非线性的决策区域"
msgstr "Just 3 neurons are sufficient to form non-convex, non-linear decision regions"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:156
msgid "这说明神经网络的表达能力来自**非线性组合**，而非单纯增加神经元数量"
msgstr "This indicates that neural network expressiveness comes from **non-linear combinations**, rather than merely increasing neuron count"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:157
msgid "深度（多层非线性组合）比宽度（单层神经元数量）更重要"
msgstr "Depth (multi-layer non-linear combination) is more important than width (single-layer neuron count)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:159
msgid ""
"**关键结论**：非线性激活函数让神经网络能够将简单的线性决策边界**组合、变换、叠加**成任意复杂的形状。没有非线性激活，无论多少层都只能学习线性分类器：$f(W_2(W_1x))"
" = W_2W_1x = W'x$。"
msgstr ""
"**Key Takeaway**: Non-linear activation functions allow neural networks to **combine, transform, and superimpose** simple linear decision boundaries into arbitrarily complex shapes. Without non-linear activation functions, no matter how many layers are used, the network can only learn a linear classifier: $f(W_2(W_1x)) = W_2W_1x = W'x$."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:165
#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:184
msgid "Sigmoid 函数"
msgstr "Sigmoid Function"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:167
msgid "Sigmoid 将任意实数映射到$(0,1)$，提供平滑的非线性变换："
msgstr "Sigmoid maps any real number into $(0, 1)$, providing a smooth non-linear transformation:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:169
msgid "\\sigma(x) = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-x}}"
msgstr "\\sigma(x) = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-x}}"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:171
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**导数**：$\\sigma'(x) = \\sigma(x)(1 - "
"\\sigma(x))$，在$x=0$处最大值为$0.25$。这个导数形式在{ref}`back-propagation`中非常重要。"
msgstr ""
"**Derivative**: $\\sigma'(x) = \\sigma(x)(1 - \\sigma(x))$, with a maximum value of $0.25$ at $x=0$. This derivative form plays a crucial role in {ref}`back-propagation`."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:173
msgid "**优点**："
msgstr "**Advantages**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:175
msgid "输出可解释为概率"
msgstr "Outputs can be interpreted as probabilities"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:176
msgid "平滑可导"
msgstr "Smooth and differentiable"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:178
msgid "**局限性**："
msgstr "**Limitations**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:180
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**梯度消失**：$|x|$较大时梯度接近0，这会导致{ref}`back-propagation`时梯度衰减"
msgstr "**Vanishing Gradient**: When $|x|$ is large, the gradient approaches 0, causing gradient decay during {ref}`back-propagation`."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:181
msgid "**非零中心**：输出始终为正"
msgstr "**Not Zero-Centered**: Outputs are always positive"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:199
msgid "Tanh函数（双曲正切）"
msgstr "Tanh Function (Hyperbolic Tangent)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:201
msgid "Tanh 是 Sigmoid 的\"零中心\"版本："
msgstr "Tanh is a \"zero-centered\" version of Sigmoid:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:203
msgid "\\tanh(x) = \\frac{e^x - e^{-x}}{e^x + e^{-x}} = 2\\sigma(2x) - 1"
msgstr "\\tanh(x) = \\frac{e^x - e^{-x}}{e^x + e^{-x}} = 2\\sigma(2x) - 1"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:205
msgid "**导数**：$\\tanh'(x) = 1 - \\tanh^2(x)$，在$x=0$处最大值为$1$"
msgstr "**Derivative**: $\\tanh'(x) = 1 - \\tanh^2(x)$, with a maximum value of $1$ at $x=0$"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:207
msgid "**相比 Sigmoid 的优势**："
msgstr "**Advantages over Sigmoid**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:209
msgid "零中心输出（-1到1）"
msgstr "Zero-centered output (-1 to 1)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:210
msgid "更强梯度信号（最大梯度是 Sigmoid 的4倍）"
msgstr "Stronger gradient signal (maximum gradient is 4 times that of Sigmoid)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:212
msgid "**局限**：仍然存在梯度消失问题"
msgstr "**Limitations**: Still suffers from vanishing gradients"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:215
msgid "Tanh函数"
msgstr "Tanh Function"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:226
msgid "ReLU 函数（Rectified Linear Unit）"
msgstr "ReLU Function (Rectified Linear Unit)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:228
#, python-brace-format
msgid "ReLU {cite}`nair2010rectified` 于2012年 AlexNet 的成功后成为主流："
msgstr "ReLU {cite}`nair2010rectified` became mainstream following the success of AlexNet in 2012:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:230
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\text{ReLU}(x) = \\max(0, x) = \\begin{cases} x & x > 0 \\\\ 0 & x \\leq"
" 0 \\end{cases}"
msgstr ""
"\\text{ReLU}(x) = \\max(0, x) = \\begin{cases} x & x > 0 \\\\ 0 & x \\leq"
" 0 \\end{cases}"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:232
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**导数**：$\\text{ReLU}'(x) = \\begin{cases} 1 & x > 0 \\\\ 0 & x < 0 "
"\\end{cases}$"
msgstr ""
"**Derivative**: $\\text{ReLU}'(x) = \\begin{cases} 1 & x > 0 \\\\ 0 & x < 0 "
"\\end{cases}$"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:234
msgid "**核心优势**："
msgstr "**Core Advantages**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:236
msgid "**解决梯度消失**：正区间梯度恒为 1"
msgstr "**Mitigates Vanishing Gradient**: Gradient is constantly 1 in the positive region"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:237
msgid "**计算高效**：仅需比较操作"
msgstr "**Computationally Efficient**: Requires only a threshold operation"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:238
msgid "**稀疏激活**：约 50% 神经元输出为 0"
msgstr "**Sparse Activation**: Roughly 50% of neurons output 0"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:240
msgid "**问题**：**\"死亡神经元\"**——若输入始终为负，梯度永远为 0，神经元永久失活"
msgstr "**Issue**: **\"Dying ReLU\"**—if inputs remain negative, gradients stay 0 permanently, deactivating the neuron indefinitely"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:243
msgid "ReLU 函数"
msgstr "ReLU Function"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:256
msgid "Leaky ReLU 与变体"
msgstr "Leaky ReLU and Variants"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:258
msgid "为解决死亡神经元问题，Leaky ReLU 给负区间一个小斜率："
msgstr "To address the dying ReLU problem, Leaky ReLU assigns a small slope to the negative region:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:260
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\text{LeakyReLU}(x) = \\begin{cases} x & x > 0 \\\\ \\alpha x & x \\leq "
"0 \\end{cases}"
msgstr ""
"\\text{LeakyReLU}(x) = \\begin{cases} x & x > 0 \\\\ \\alpha x & x \\leq "
"0 \\end{cases}"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:262
msgid "其中 $\\alpha$ 通常取 0.01。"
msgstr "where $\\alpha$ is typically set to 0.01."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:264
msgid "**优势**："
msgstr "**Advantages**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:266
msgid "负区间有非零梯度，防止神经元死亡"
msgstr "Non-zero gradient in the negative region prevents dying neurons"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:267
msgid "保持 ReLU 的计算效率"
msgstr "Retains the computational efficiency of ReLU"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:269
msgid "**进阶变体**："
msgstr "**Advanced Variants**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:271
msgid "**PReLU**：$\\alpha$ 作为可学习参数"
msgstr "**PReLU**: $\\alpha$ treated as a learnable parameter"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:272
msgid "**ELU**：负区间使用指数函数，更平滑"
msgstr "**ELU**: Uses an exponential function in the negative region for smoothness"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:275
msgid "Leaky ReLU函数"
msgstr "Leaky ReLU Function"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:289
#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:311
msgid "Swish 函数"
msgstr "Swish Function"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:291
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"由 Google Brain 团队的 Prajit Ramachandran 等人于 2017 年通过神经架构搜索发现 "
"{cite}`ramachandran2017swish`。其设计动机体现了深度学习研究的新趋势：**通过自动化方法发现新的激活函数**"
msgstr ""
"Discovered in 2017 by Prajit Ramachandran et al. at Google Brain using neural architecture search {cite}`ramachandran2017swish`. Its design reflects a modern trend in deep learning research: **discovering new activation functions through automated methods**."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:293
msgid ""
" \\text{Swish}(x) = x \\cdot \\sigma(\\beta x) = \\frac{x}{1 + e^{-\\beta"
" x}} "
msgstr ""
" \\text{Swish}(x) = x \\cdot \\sigma(\\beta x) = \\frac{x}{1 + e^{-\\beta"
" x}} "

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:295
msgid "其中 $\\beta$ 是可选的可学习参数（通常取 1.0）。"
msgstr "where $\\beta$ is an optional learnable parameter (usually set to 1.0)."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:297
msgid "**性质**："
msgstr "**Properties**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:299
msgid ""
"**自门控机制**：Swish 将输入 $x$ 作为\"门\"，将 $\\sigma(\\beta x)$ 作为\"门控信号\"，实现 $x$ 与"
" $\\sigma(\\beta x)$ 的逐元素相乘"
msgstr ""
"**Self-Gating Mechanism**: Swish treats input $x$ as the gate and $\\sigma(\\beta x)$ as the gating signal, computing element-wise multiplication between $x$ and $\\sigma(\\beta x)$."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:300
msgid "**平滑非单调**：与 ReLU 不同，Swish 是非单调的，在负区间有小的负值"
msgstr "**Smooth Non-Monotonic**: Unlike ReLU, Swish is non-monotonic and exhibits a small negative dip in the negative domain."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:301
msgid "**可学习参数**：$\\beta$ 可以设置为可学习的参数，让网络自动调整门控强度"
msgstr "**Learnable Parameter**: $\\beta$ can be trained, allowing the network to adaptively adjust gating intensity."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:302
msgid "**实验验证**：通过大规模实验验证，Swish 在多个任务上优于 ReLU"
msgstr "**Empirical Validation**: Extensively verified through experiments to outperform ReLU across multiple tasks."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:304
msgid "**与ReLU的关系**"
msgstr "**Relationship with ReLU**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:306
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"当 $\\beta \\to \\infty$ 时，$\\sigma(\\beta x) \\to \\text{step}(x)$，Swish "
"趋近于 ReLU："
msgstr ""
"As $\\beta \\to \\infty$, $\\sigma(\\beta x) \\to \\text{step}(x)$, and Swish approaches ReLU:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:308
msgid ""
" \\lim_{\\beta \\to \\infty} \\frac{x}{1 + e^{-\\beta x}} = "
"\\begin{cases} x & \\text{if } x > 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{otherwise} "
"\\end{cases} "
msgstr ""
" \\lim_{\\beta \\to \\infty} \\frac{x}{1 + e^{-\\beta x}} = "
"\\begin{cases} x & \\text{if } x > 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{otherwise} "
"\\end{cases} "

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:321
msgid "Softmax 函数"
msgstr "Softmax Function"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:323
msgid "Softmax 是多分类问题的标准输出层激活函数，将 logits 转换为概率分布："
msgstr "Softmax is the standard output layer activation function for multi-class classification, converting logits into a probability distribution:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:325
msgid "\\text{softmax}(x_i) = \\frac{e^{x_i}}{\\sum_{j=1}^C e^{x_j}}"
msgstr "\\text{softmax}(x_i) = \\frac{e^{x_i}}{\\sum_{j=1}^C e^{x_j}}"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:327
msgid "**关键性质**："
msgstr "**Key Properties**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:329
msgid "输出和为 1，可解释为概率"
msgstr "Outputs sum to 1 and can be interpreted as probabilities"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:330
msgid "指数放大差异：高分更高，低分更低"
msgstr "Exponentially amplifies differences: high scores become higher, low scores lower"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:331
msgid "类别之间应该是\"竞争\"的，一个类别的概率增加意味着其他类别概率降低"
msgstr "Classes are mutually competitive: an increase in one class probability decreases others"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:333
msgid "**与交叉熵损失配合**："
msgstr "**Interplay with Cross-Entropy Loss**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:335
#, python-brace-format
msgid "梯度形式简洁：$\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial x_i} = \\text{softmax}(x_i) - y_i$"
msgstr "Concise gradient form: $\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial x_i} = \\text{softmax}(x_i) - y_i$"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/activation-functions.md:338
msgid "Softmax 变换示意"
msgstr "Softmax Transformation Diagram"

